---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy | cppMax" description="What cppMax keeps on your device and when optional services use the network.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="The compiler does not need your code in the cloud." description="cppMax is designed to edit, compile, and run projects on your device. This draft describes the current beta." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell policy-layout">
    <aside><strong>Draft notice</strong><span>Updated August 29, 2026</span><p>This notice will expand before the public App Store release.</p></aside>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Code and project files</h2><p>The editor reads and writes project files on your device. Clang and LLD compile those files locally. cppMax does not need to send source code or compiled programs to a cppMax server for the build and run loop.</p>
      <h2>Signing data</h2><p>cppMax uses the executable's SHA-256 hash to identify a signed build. The current beta performs automatic signing. This notice will be updated with storage and service details before post-beta signing or envToken services launch.</p>
      <h2>When the network is used</h2><p>Core editing and compilation can work offline. These optional actions use a connection:</p><ul><li>Cloning, pulling, or pushing a remote Git repository</li><li>Opening a support channel or public issue tracker</li><li>Earning envTokens through the planned advertising option</li><li>Checking for app or beta updates</li></ul><p>Third-party services have their own privacy terms.</p>
      <h2>Diagnostics and support</h2><p>Review logs before sharing them. Remove source code, file paths, credentials, and personal information that support staff do not need to reproduce the problem.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2><p>The update date at the top of this page will change when the notice changes. The final policy will identify the app operator, contact method, service providers, retention periods, and user rights before public release.</p>
      <h2>Questions</h2><p>The current contact status is listed on the <a class="text-link" href="/support/">support page</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .policy-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr; gap: 90px; align-items: start; }
  .policy-layout aside { position: sticky; top: 105px; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .policy-layout aside strong, .policy-layout aside span { display: block; }
  .policy-layout aside strong { margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--orange); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .policy-layout aside span { font-weight: 750; }
  .policy-layout aside p { margin: 24px 0 0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .policy-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 45px; } .policy-layout aside { position: static; } }
</style>
